# 1. Purpose

The Documentation Standard defines the canonical requirements for producing, organizing, and maintaining documentation within Kaivo Core.

It establishes a consistent documentation structure that preserves clarity, traceability, and compatibility across all canonical artifacts.

---

# 2. Scope

The Documentation Standard defines:

* Documentation principles.
* Documentation structure.
* Documentation consistency requirements.
* Documentation boundaries.
* Conformance requirements.

The Documentation Standard does not define:

* Repository implementation.
* Source control workflows.
* Architecture redesign.
* Runtime behavior.
* Technical implementation.

---

# 3. Documentation Principles

Documentation shall be:

* Canonical.
* Consistent.
* Complete.
* Traceable.
* Readable.
* Stable.
* Implementation-neutral.

---

# 4. Documentation Requirements

Every canonical document shall:

* Possess a unique Document ID.
* Possess a canonical title.
* Identify its artifact type.
* Specify its authority.
* Specify its version.
* Declare its dependencies when applicable.
* Preserve approved canonical terminology.

---

# 5. Structural Requirements

Every canonical document shall follow a consistent structure appropriate to its artifact type.

The structure shall:

* Clearly identify the artifact.
* Define its purpose.
* Define its scope.
* Present normative content.
* Identify normative references.
* Conclude with the current lifecycle status.

---

# 6. Documentation Principles for Maintenance

Documentation shall:

* Preserve approved canonical terminology.
* Maintain consistency across related artifacts.
* Preserve traceability.
* Remain compatible with approved governance policies.

---

# 7. Boundaries

The Documentation Standard does not define:

* Repository organization.
* Release management.
* Organizational procedures.
* Runtime execution.
* Implementation technologies.

---

# 8. Canonical Constraints

### C1

Every canonical document shall possess exactly one canonical identifier.

---

### C2

Documentation shall preserve approved canonical terminology.

---

### C3

Documentation shall maintain consistency with approved canonical artifacts.

---

### C4

Documentation shall preserve traceability throughout the document lifecycle.

---

### C5

Documentation shall conform to the Naming Convention Standard.

---

### C6

The Documentation Standard shall conform to the Core Ontology.

---

### C7

The Documentation Standard shall conform to the Core Asset Model.

---

# 9. Conformance

A document conforms to this standard if it:

* Applies the required documentation structure.
* Preserves approved canonical terminology.
* Maintains consistency with approved artifacts.
* Preserves traceability.
* Conforms to the Governance Charter.
* Conforms to the Naming Convention Standard.

